Auto-split child 3/4 of claudego-ec6d3ae3 (umbrella). Blocked by the reserve-policy acceptance-tests child — document the behaviour the tests have pinned, not an intended one.

CONTEXT: the affinity change alters what docs/notes/human-reserve-policy.md promises (a premium window's risk no longer caps pools that cannot consume it) and how weekly saturation is achieved (docs/notes/weekly-saturation.md). Undocumented, the next operator or agent will read the old policy and misread live behaviour as a bug — or the new one as a reserve-policy violation.

SCOPE — update docs/notes/human-reserve-policy.md and docs/notes/weekly-saturation.md to describe:
- per-pool cap = min safe_worker_count across the pool's declared windows (AgentConfig.windows / consumed_windows() in src/config.rs; pool_window_safe_cap in src/governor.rs);
- binding-window selection restricted to the intersection of enabled pools' declared windows (fleet_binding_affinity); undeclared = assumed ALL windows (conservative, pre-fix behaviour); empty/unknown declarations fall back the same way;
- the >=98% emergency brake remains GLOBAL and unchanged — the human reserve is not weakened;
- an example governor.yaml snippet declaring windows: [five_hour, seven_day] for the needle-sonnet pool (config lives at ~/.config/claude-governor/governor.yaml, machine-specific, NOT in this repo);
- the incident motivating this: weekly_scoped risk holding the Sonnet fleet at 0, observed 2026-09-07 while enabling enforcement (claudego-80eb5eea), tracked as claudego-ec6d3ae3.

ACCEPTANCE: docs match the landed code and pinned tests (correct function/field/flag names); no credential values anywhere; committed to main with precise paths and pushed to Forgejo origin.

Found 2026-09-08 while closing claudego-46d8787b: cargo test (target level) fails to compile tests/hysteresis_smooth_scaling_test.rs, so no full cargo test pass can succeed on this repo.

Evidence:
  error[E0432]: unresolved import cgov
    --> tests/hysteresis_smooth_scaling_test.rs:11:5
  11 | use cgov::governor::{apply_scaling, compute_target_workers, ScalingDecision};
  12 | use cgov::config::{CompositeRiskConfig, ConeScalingConfig};
  13 | use cgov::state;

Cargo.toml declares [lib] name = "claude_governor" (only the [[bin]] is named cgov), so the three imports must be claude_governor::... . The file has been broken since it landed in e00b963 (2026-08-23, 'docs: comprehensive hysteresis and smooth scaling documentation'); it went unnoticed because it is an integration-test target, not lib tests — cargo test --lib passes all 792.

Scope: fix the three imports (and optionally the rustfmt diffs in the same file, which predate this), then confirm cargo test --test hysteresis_smooth_scaling_test compiles and passes. Do not change governor.rs/config.rs/state.rs behaviour to make it pass — if any assertion in the file is wrong against current behaviour, split that out rather than weakening it.

Not covered by any open bead (checked 2026-09-08).

In run_governor_cycle (around lines 2011-2040), ensure proper Option pattern matching:

- Modify the if let pattern to clearly handle Option<PreviousSnapshot> types
- Ensure code gracefully handles when previous_api_snapshot is None
- Add clear early return or skip logic for first poll case

The pattern should be:
```rust
if let (Some(prev), Some(curr)) = (&state.previous_api_snapshot, &state.current_api_snapshot) {
    // Compute deltas only when both snapshots exist
} else {
    // First poll or missing data - skip delta computation
    // Explicitly set delta fields to None or 0.0
}
```

Acceptance criteria:
- Pattern matches on Option types correctly
- Code compiles without errors
- First poll case (prev_snapshot is None) is handled gracefully
